<title>UK: Despairing British gambler wins $500,000.</title>
<headline>Despairing British gambler wins $500,000.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A British gambler who won over 300,000 pounds ($500,000) from a one-pound bet had forgotten which horse he had backed and stormed out of the bookmakers in despair after watching the race on television.</p>
<p>It was only when he returned to the betting shop six days later that staff told him of his win in the seven-race accumulator, bookmaker Ladbrokes said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;I was very shocked, but it's beginning to sink in now,&quot; said the winner, chef Brian Green. ($1=.6298 Pound)</p>
</text>
